# Chrome overlays

Dialogs, menus, and popovers must stay inside the viewport. Title, tabs, and footer actions stay visible. The content region is the only scroller.

```css
/* ❌ BAD — shell clips; body never shrinks so overflow:auto never runs */
.dialog {
  max-height: 32rem;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.body {
  overflow: auto;
}

/* ✅ GOOD — cap to the viewport; chrome does not shrink; body is the scrollport */
.dialog {
  max-width: 100%;
  max-height: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.header, .tabs, .actions {
  flex-shrink: 0;
}
.body {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-height: 0;
  overflow: auto;
}
```

Do not hardcode a pixel height that can exceed the viewport. Prefer `max-height: 100%` (padded backdrop) or `min(24rem, calc(100vh - 8px))` for lists and pickers. `overflow: hidden` on the shell is OK only when a child is the scrollport.

Flyout menus (toolbar pulldowns and submenus) must keep `overflow: visible` so a `position: absolute` submenu can paint at `left: 100%`. Do not put `overflow: auto` on a menu that hosts flyouts — CSS cannot combine `overflow-y: auto` with `overflow-x: visible`.

```css
/* ❌ BAD — clips File/Edit flyouts inside a 10rem scroll box */
.menu { overflow: auto; }

/* ✅ GOOD — submenu can sit beside the parent */
.menu { overflow: visible; }
```
